<h2>Control rendering and input order</h2>
<p><code>corner_radius</code> rounds native panel/control fills and borders. Text inputs apply their padding to placeholder text, entered text, selection, composition and caret, and honor vertical text alignment. Sliders render a narrow track with a thumb; progress controls fill their authored bounds.</p>
<p>Pointer hit testing follows the same effective layer order as rendering, including inherited visibility and scroll clipping. <code>focusable: false</code> removes a control from keyboard focus traversal while retaining pointer activation. This is useful for a transparent outside-click target behind a popup; set both its background and hover colors transparent.</p>
